<title>ITALY: Magneti Marelli 1996 profits rise.</title>
<headline>Magneti Marelli 1996 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian automotive components group Magneti Marelli, controlled by Fiat, on Tuesday reported consolidated net profits rose to 58 billion lire in 1996 from 54 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>A group statement said net profits of the parent company fell to 53.7 billion lire from 62.5 billion lire, and the dividend was unchanged for 1996 at 80 lire per ordinary share and 100 lire per savings share.</p>
<p>Annual sales in 1996 rose 4.6 percent to 5.806 trillion lire while net debt increased to 205 billion lire at end-1996 from 184 billion lire at end-1995.</p>
<p>In the first three months of 1997, the group sales rose 6.1 percent to 1.620 trillion lire, operating profits were 18 billion lire after 10 billion lire, and pretax profits were nine billion lire, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129052</p>
